        "original_id": "6c713d90-7dbe-54b2-beb3-7d694a879737",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Companies: Pacific Film Unit, Pacific Film Productions Ltd, Pacific Films\n- People: Alun Falconer, Roger Mirams, John O'Shea, John Francis O'Shea\n- Organizations: National Film Unit, Republic of Ireland national team, Sunderland\n- Places: Wellington, New Zealand, China\n- Roles: producer, defender, vice-captain\n- Products: The Coastwatchers\n- Topics: coastwatchers\n\nFacts:\n- In 1948, Alun Falconer and Roger Mirams, who were former National Film Unit staff, established the Pacific Film Unit in Wellington, New Zealand.\n- In 1950, John O'Shea joined the Pacific Film Unit, Alun Falconer left to pursue a career in China, and the company changed its name to Pacific Film Productions Ltd.\n- In 1959, producer Roger Mirams made The Coastwatchers, a TV docudrama about coastwatchers, for Pacific Films.\n- John Francis O'Shea was born on 30 April 1981.\n- John Francis O'Shea is an Irish footballer who plays as a defender for Sunderland and the Republic of Ireland national team.\n- John Francis O'Shea serves as vice-captain of the Republic of Ireland national team.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "17b8524c-618a-5bd9-998d-854a91ce164d",
        "text": "Page: Pacific Films. Sentence: The Pacific Film Unit was established in Wellington, New Zealand in 1948 by ex-National Film Unit staff Alun Falconer and Roger Mirams.\nPage: Pacific Films. Sentence: In 1950 John O'Shea joined; Falconer left to pursue a career in China; and the company changed its name to Pacific Film Productions Ltd.\nPage: John O'Shea. Sentence: John Francis O'Shea (born 30 April 1981) is an Irish footballer, who plays as a defender for Sunderland and the Republic of Ireland national team, where he serves as vice-captain.\nPage: The Coastwatchers (TV movie). Sentence: The Coastwatchers was a TV docudrama about coastwatchers made in 1959 by producer Roger Mirams for Pacific Films.",
        "type": "DocumentChunk"
